Argh, now I have to choose between nethack and netrek...

The new X interface to nethack is slick, works
nice, I'm very impressed.

I had to comment out the definitions of sleep in the
system.h file to make things compile nicely, other
than that, no probs.  (ultrix 4.3, with cc, but I
remember having to do this for 3.0 as well, under
older versions of ultrix.

For me, the easiest way to handle the Nethack.ad file was
to just incorporate it into my .Xdefaults, or .Xresources.
If you use .Xdefaults, you'll have to change the beginning
'!'s to '#'s.  If you use .Xresources, make sure you do:
xrdb -merge ~/.Xresources to make it current, unless you logout
and back in again.

All in all, very nicely done guys.
